      "body": "## Motivation\n\nIn `LightOnOCRProcessor.process_mm_data_async` (`python/sglang/srt/multimodal/processors/lightonocr.py`), removing Pixtral row-break and image-end tokens previously:\n1. Allocated an $O(L)$ Python dictionary `old_to_new` mapping every surviving token position `old_idx -> new_idx`.\n2. For each multimodal item, iterated over **every individual token index** `idx in range(start, end + 1)` across all `(start, end)` row spans in `mm_item.offsets`, looked up `old_to_new[idx]`, materialized the full list of thousands of remapped token indices, and called `sorted(...)` just to read `(new_indices[0], new_indices[-1])`.\n3. Left stale un-remapped `mm_item.offsets` in place if all tokens inside `mm_item.offsets` were removed (`new_indices` empty).\n\nFor multi-page OCR workloads (e.g., 8 pages at $64 \\times 64$ patches = 33,291 tokens), this dictionary construction + per-token expansion + sort adds unnecessary CPU overhead on every multimodal request.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Replace the `old_to_new` dictionary with a contiguous `surviving_old_indices` list of surviving token indices (which is naturally strictly increasing).\n- Use `bisect_left(surviving_old_indices, start)` and `bisect_right(surviving_old_indices, end) - 1` on each `(start, end)` span endpoint in `mm_item.offsets` to find the remapped `[min_new_idx, max_new_idx]` bounds in $O(R \\log L)$ time without iterating over or sorting individual patch token indices.\n- Clear `mm_item.offsets = []` when all tokens in `mm_item.offsets` are removed.\n- Add unit tests in `test/registered/unit/multimodal/test_lightonocr_processor.py`.\n\n### Micro-benchmark (8-page $64 \\times 64$ document, 33,291 tokens)\n- **Before**: `10.67 ms`\n- **After**: `3.52 ms` (**3.03x speedup**)\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format Guide](https://docs.sglang.io/references/contribution_guide.html#format-your-code).\n- [x] Add unit tests as outlined in the [Contribution Guide](https://docs.sglang.io/references/contribution_guide.html#running-unit-tests-and-adding-new-tests).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:warning: [Run #41801184186](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41801184186)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:warning: [Run #41801184029](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41801184029)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:warning: [Run #41801184040](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41801184040)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
